<resources>
    <!-- ★ THIS TABLET HAS NO NOTIFICATION LED. Owner-confirmed, session 21.

         lineage-sdk defaults this to 8 = LIGHTS_PULSATING_LED
         (lineage-sdk/lineage/res/res/values/config.xml:98), and
         LightsCapabilities.java:56,62 is what reads it. Left at the default,
         LineageOS offers notification-light settings for hardware that does not
         exist, and every one of them does nothing.

         ⚠️ The evidence pointed the other way, which is exactly why this needed
         asking rather than deducing. /sys/class/leds/ has `blue` and `green`,
         both with max_brightness 255, and on the stock ROM `green` reads 255
         while charging — a textbook charge-LED signature. A QTI lights HAL is
         installed and android.hardware.light@2 ILights/default is registered.

         None of that is evidence about THIS model. Lenovo ships one vendor
         image across several SKUs, so /vendor carries drivers and HAL services
         for hardware this tablet does not have. The vibrator is the same story
         told once already: complete live stack, registered IVibrator, nine
         primitives, a real PMIC node — and no motor. See OPEN-ISSUES.md #6, #14.

         0 = no light capabilities at all. -->
    <integer name="config_deviceLightCapabilities">0</integer>
</resources>
